      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not change your dosage or timing without consulting your doctor first. Dizziness when standing up quickly is a common side effect of blood pressure medication and is usually related to changes in blood pressure. Instead of doubling up, try standing up slowly and gradually when you get out of bed or a chair. If the lightheadedness persists, it's important to tell your prescribing physician so they can adjust your treatment plan safely.",
